---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../site.config";
import { pathTo } from "../lib/paths";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" narrow>
  <article class="prose">
    <header class="doc-header">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="doc-meta">Last updated: {site.lastUpdated}</p>
    </header>

    <p>
      {site.name} (“we,” “us,” or “our”) provides a document scanning app for iPhone, iPad, Android, and HarmonyOS devices. This Privacy Policy explains what
      information is processed when you use {site.name} and the choices you have.
    </p>

    <div class="summary">
      <p>
        <strong>Summary:</strong> {site.name} helps you scan documents and create PDFs on your device. You do not need an account.
        Your scans and PDFs stay in the app unless you export or share them. Optional product analytics are off by default and
        never include the contents of your documents. {site.name} does not sell your personal information or use your scans for
        advertising.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} is published under the name <strong>{site.name}</strong> on the App Store. If you have questions about this
      policy, contact us using the support email listed on the {site.name} App Store page (recommended subject:{" "}
      <strong>{site.name} — Privacy</strong>).
    </p>

    <h2>2. Scope</h2>
    <p>
      This policy applies to the {site.name} mobile apps on iOS, Android, and HarmonyOS and the features described below. It does not cover third-party services you
      choose when exporting or sharing (for example Mail, cloud storage, or messaging apps), or websites we do not operate.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Information we process</h2>

    <h3>3.1 Documents and PDFs</h3>
    <p>
      When you scan with the camera, import photos, edit pages, or create PDFs, {site.name} stores those files locally in the
      app’s private storage on your device. We do not automatically upload your scans, images, or PDFs to our servers. {site.name}{" "}
      does not provide automatic cloud sync or an account-based backup service.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you use iPhone or iPad backup (such as iCloud Backup or a computer backup), Apple may include app data in that backup
      according to your device settings.
    </p>
    <p>
      When you share or save a PDF with the system share sheet or Files, you choose where copies go. Those copies are outside{" "}
      {site.name}. If you delete a document in {site.name}, we remove {site.name}’s copies on your device; we cannot delete
      files you already saved or shared elsewhere.
    </p>

    <h3>3.2 Camera and Photo Library</h3>
    <p>{site.name} requests access only when needed:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Camera</strong> — to capture document scans. Camera data is used for scanning and is not uploaded automatically.</li>
      <li><strong>Photo Library</strong> — to import photos you select. Only the items you choose are added to a document.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Images remain on your device unless you export or share them.</p>

    <h3>3.3 Optional analytics</h3>
    <p>
      Product analytics are <strong>disabled by default</strong>. If you turn analytics <strong>on</strong> in Welcome or
      Settings, {site.name} may send anonymous usage events to help us understand whether features work (for example, whether a
      scan or PDF export completed). If you turn analytics off or decline opt-in, we stop sending analytics events, including any
      events that were queued while you were offline.
    </p>
    <p>When analytics are enabled, events may include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>General event types (for example, scan started, scan completed, PDF export completed, share sheet opened).</li>
      <li>Coarse ranges only (for example, number of pages in ranges such as 1, 2–5, or 6+; approximate duration or file-size ranges).</li>
      <li>Standard failure categories — not the text of errors or your documents.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Analytics do <strong>not</strong> include document titles, text on pages, images, file paths, filenames tied to your
      content, or your name or email. {site.name} has no sign-in account.
    </p>
    <p>
      We may use <strong>Google Firebase Analytics</strong> as our analytics provider when you have opted in. Google processes
      data according to <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google’s Privacy Policy</a>.
      Firebase may also record standard session-related signals while collection is enabled. We use analytics to improve the app,
      not for cross-app advertising tracking.
    </p>
    <p>You can change your analytics preference anytime in Settings.</p>

    <h3>3.4 Feedback</h3>
    <p>
      Settings includes <strong>Send feedback</strong>. Text you enter is stored on your device unless you choose to share it
      outside the app. Optional attachments require your confirmation; the app does not automatically attach your document library
      or scans.
    </p>
    <p>If you email us separately, we receive whatever information you include in your message.</p>

    <h3>3.5 App settings</h3>
    <p>
      {site.name} stores preferences on your device (for example, whether you completed welcome and your analytics choice). This
      is used to run the app, not for advertising.
    </p>

    <h3>3.6 What we do not collect</h3>
    <p>
      {site.name} does not require a user account. We do not collect contact information through the app unless you contact us
      voluntarily. We do not use the advertising identifier (IDFA) or track you across other companies’ apps and websites for
      advertising. This version of {site.name} does not perform OCR or send your documents to the cloud for processing. We do not
      sell your personal information.
    </p>

    <h2>4. How we use information</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Information</th>
          <th>Purpose</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Scans, edits, and PDFs</td>
          <td>Provide scanning and PDF features on your device</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Camera and selected photos</td>
          <td>Capture and import pages you choose</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Optional analytics</td>
          <td>Understand feature usage and reliability <strong>only if you opt in</strong></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Feedback you save</td>
          <td>Let you prepare feedback on your device</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Settings and consent</td>
          <td>Remember your choices</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>5. Legal bases (EEA, UK, and similar regions)</h2>
    <p>Where applicable law requires a legal basis:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Performance of the service / legitimate interests</strong> — processing on your device to provide scanning and PDF features you use.</li>
      <li><strong>Consent</strong> — optional analytics, which you can withdraw in Settings.</li>
      <li><strong>Legitimate interests</strong> — responding to support messages you send us.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Apple</strong> — {site.name} runs on iOS and uses Apple system services (camera, photo picker, share sheet, and
      file export). Apple’s terms and privacy practices apply to your device and any Apple backup or iCloud features you enable.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Google (Firebase Analytics)</strong> — only when you opt in to analytics, as described in Section 3.3.
    </p>
    <p>{site.name} does not automatically sync your documents to third-party cloud storage services.</p>

    <h2>7. Retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      You can delete individual documents or your entire local library from in-app controls. That removes {site.name}’s files from
      the app on your device.
    </p>
    <p>
      When analytics are off, no new analytics events are sent. Your analytics choice is stored on the device so we can honor it
      when you reopen the app.
    </p>
    <p>On-device feedback remains until you delete the app or clear that data.</p>
    <p>If you email us, we keep messages only as long as needed to respond and for ordinary record-keeping.</p>

    <h2>8. Security</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} keeps documents in the iOS app sandbox. Apple provides device encryption when you use a passcode or equivalent.
      No storage or transmission method is completely secure; we design optional analytics so document content is not included in
      analytics events.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Children</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} is not directed at children under 13 (or the minimum age required in your country). We do not knowingly collect
      personal information from children. If you believe a child has contacted us with personal information, please reach out
      through the App Store support email and we will take appropriate steps.
    </p>

    <h2>10. International use</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} is available in multiple countries. Your documents are processed primarily on your device. If you opt in to
      analytics, our analytics provider may process event data in countries where it operates.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Your rights and choices</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or restrict processing, or to object or
      withdraw consent. You can delete document data in the app. You can turn off analytics in Settings. For other requests,
      contact us using the support email on the App Store listing.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>California residents:</strong> We do not sell personal information as defined under the CCPA/CPRA for the practices
      described in this policy.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Tracking</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} does not use your data to track you across apps and websites owned by other companies for advertising. We do not
      integrate advertising SDKs that rely on the advertising identifier for cross-app tracking.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy when our practices or legal requirements change. If we make material changes to how
      optional analytics works, we will update the in-app notice and consent where required. The “Last updated” date at the top
      shows when this policy was last revised. Continued use of {site.name} after an update means you accept the revised policy,
      subject to applicable law and any new consent we ask for optional analytics.
    </p>

    <h2>14. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For privacy questions or requests, email us at the <strong>support address shown on the {site.name} App Store page</strong>.
      Please include “Privacy” in the subject line so we can route your message.
    </p>

    <nav class="prose-nav" aria-label="Related">
      <a href={pathTo("/support")}>Help &amp; Support</a>
      <a href={pathTo("/")}>Back to home</a>
    </nav>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
